1
00:00:10,190 --> 00:00:14,690
S3 has more than one name. Kulhari. Monarch.

2
00:00:17,540 --> 00:00:22,190
S3 means Surai 3. Surai is a zone in Pilibhit.

3
00:00:23,790 --> 00:00:28,240
There was also an S2. S2 and S3 fought near the main road.

4
00:00:28,290 --> 00:00:34,140
S2 left S3 so badly hurt that forest officers had to save him.

5
00:00:35,540 --> 00:00:41,190
He was kept for recovery, then released back into the jungle.

6
00:00:41,240 --> 00:00:45,965
That fight had happened a year before our trip.

7
00:00:47,340 --> 00:00:48,330
First time I saw S3: 4:56 PM.

8
00:00:48,380 --> 00:00:51,240
Our safari was ending at 5:00.

9
00:00:51,290 --> 00:00:56,690
Four minutes to see the tiger and race to the exit gate.

10
00:00:59,150 --> 00:01:01,390
But it was not S3. It was Rocket.

11
00:01:01,440 --> 00:01:05,865
Rocket is a very famous tiger of that area.

12
00:01:06,290 --> 00:01:08,540
He has not been seen this year.

13
00:01:08,590 --> 00:01:14,065
His father was Barahi male. Barahi is a zone, like Surai.

14
00:01:23,640 --> 00:01:28,440
Barahi male vanished. I think I saw him in 2024.

15
00:01:29,540 --> 00:01:34,565
Why Rocket? A rocket-shaped mark above his eyebrow.

16
00:01:38,712 --> 00:01:43,512
In our sighting, Rocket came walking towards us.

17
00:01:46,620 --> 00:01:50,320
He walked in front of us for 30 to 60 minutes.

18
00:01:50,370 --> 00:01:51,783
Our jeep kept reversing.

19
00:01:51,833 --> 00:01:54,670
Then we saw another tiger, 200 to 250 metres behind.

20
00:01:54,720 --> 00:01:59,820
Two male tigers in one place. A fight looked likely.

21
00:02:11,020 --> 00:02:14,713
Rocket ahead. Another tiger behind. Who was it?

22
00:02:14,763 --> 00:02:17,763
S3? S2? We did not know.

23
00:02:18,070 --> 00:02:22,884
Barahi male could not be it. Not seen for 1.5 years.

24
00:02:22,934 --> 00:02:26,684
Rocket crossed over and went away.

25
00:02:26,850 --> 00:02:29,138
The second tiger walked towards us. It was S3.

26
00:02:29,188 --> 00:02:33,838
S3 is about 10 feet head to tail. My estimate.

27
00:02:38,100 --> 00:02:42,000
Listed weight: around 250 to 300 kg.

28
00:02:45,950 --> 00:02:51,875
He walked in front of us for 1 to 1.5 hours, marking territory.

29
00:02:52,250 --> 00:02:56,150
Yet S3 is considered a little timid.

30
00:02:59,600 --> 00:03:03,725
Ears back. Body low. He looked nervous.

31
00:03:12,050 --> 00:03:15,875
S3 walks on both sides of the road.

32
00:03:19,350 --> 00:03:22,050
He turns and walks the other way.

33
00:03:22,100 --> 00:03:27,800
Now we are behind him. The jeeps behind us are now in front.

34
00:03:28,300 --> 00:03:33,925
He did this many times. Everyone reversed, again and again.

35
00:03:39,430 --> 00:03:44,380
Next day: Rocket was sitting there again, relaxed.

36
00:03:54,830 --> 00:03:59,480
One jeep had engine trouble. It kept stalling.

37
00:04:00,130 --> 00:04:04,330
I told the driver: do not get us killed.

38
00:04:40,430 --> 00:04:44,930
Rocket came out and ran straight at the jeep.

39
00:04:44,980 --> 00:04:50,230
It was not a charge. It felt like one. The jeep shook.

40
00:04:53,491 --> 00:04:57,391
Only a client's phone was recording.

41
00:04:59,657 --> 00:05:04,907
He had probably caught the scent of another tiger. S3.

42
00:05:26,009 --> 00:05:31,634
He jumped as high as he could. Claw marks at 10 to 11 feet.

43
00:05:41,282 --> 00:05:45,210
A very unique behaviour of Rocket and S3.

44
00:05:45,260 --> 00:05:51,260
That rivalry has more or less ended. Rocket was not seen this year.

45
00:05:53,610 --> 00:05:58,785
Barahi female, mate of Barahi male, is now with cubs.

46
00:06:03,760 --> 00:06:07,260
A very unique sighting of Barahi female. November 2025.

47
00:06:07,310 --> 00:06:12,335
As we entered, many jeeps were already ahead of us.

48
00:06:15,460 --> 00:06:21,310
She was walking 3 to 4 km. Her route cuts the road right here.

49
00:06:22,460 --> 00:06:24,710
What do we do?

50
00:06:28,210 --> 00:06:31,360
8 to 10 jeeps ahead of us.

51
00:06:33,460 --> 00:06:35,610
Jeeps behind her. Jeeps ahead of her.

52
00:06:35,660 --> 00:06:38,885
I said: this will not work.

53
00:06:41,410 --> 00:06:43,398
How many photos can you take through one small gap?

54
00:06:43,448 --> 00:06:45,860
This is why you must understand tiger behaviour.

55
00:06:45,910 --> 00:06:50,410
Respect the tiger's time. Respect her space.

56
00:07:02,060 --> 00:07:04,960
It is her home. We are the visitors.

57
00:07:05,010 --> 00:07:09,735
Then she stepped off the track into the bushes.

58
00:07:22,360 --> 00:07:26,635
I said: give her space. She will come up.

59
00:07:31,110 --> 00:07:35,610
Take the jeeps back. As far back as you can.

60
00:07:37,860 --> 00:07:40,699
We pulled our jeep all the way back.

61
00:07:40,749 --> 00:07:45,999
Keep the maximum gap. Let her walk through the bushes.

62
00:07:48,435 --> 00:07:51,886
We had left such a big gap that the other jeeps stayed behind.

63
00:07:51,936 --> 00:07:56,736
She came out of the bushes, back onto the track.

64
00:07:57,910 --> 00:08:03,535
Only our jeep got head-on shots. Everyone else got tail-on.

65
00:08:03,960 --> 00:08:07,110
Shoot as much as you like.

66
00:08:12,560 --> 00:08:17,135
A web of jeeps behind her. Behind us, nobody.

67
00:08:18,560 --> 00:08:20,260
The guide and driver play a role too.

68
00:08:20,310 --> 00:08:26,010
She cut down again. We knew she would come out on the track.

69
00:08:27,610 --> 00:08:33,160
The driver said: park here. Nobody goes beyond this point.

70
00:08:39,410 --> 00:08:44,735
Let her pass. No disturbance. Switch off your vehicles.

71
00:08:47,143 --> 00:08:49,860
A bike was coming from behind.

72
00:08:49,910 --> 00:08:53,810
The rider saw the tiger and stopped.

73
00:08:54,110 --> 00:08:58,384
She crossed and walked into the other zone.

74
00:08:58,434 --> 00:09:02,484
The biker took a U-turn and went back.

75
00:09:08,460 --> 00:09:08,860
Because we gave her less space.

76
00:09:08,460 --> 00:09:12,735
Why did she step down in the first place?

77
00:09:14,510 --> 00:09:19,835
The jeeps behind her put pressure. They got very close.

78
00:09:26,360 --> 00:09:32,360
Engine noise. People talking. To her, all of it was disturbance.

79
00:09:35,511 --> 00:09:38,586
Always keep this in mind.

80
00:09:40,610 --> 00:09:42,230
Give full respect, and you will get good photos and videos.

